, the color code is as follows: green for $\frac{2}{3}\,Z_m \le Z \le Z_m$; red for $\frac{1}{3}\,Z_m \le Z < \frac{2}{3}\,Z_m$; and blue for $0 \le Z < \frac{1}{3}\,Z_m$. (b) Spreading time $\tau_\mathsf{\,f}$ \textit{vs} $Z$. The cyan dashed line (\textcolor{cyan}{\textbf{--\,--\,--}}) is a linear fit to the binned data (large golden dots \textcolor{Dandelion}{\Large $\bullet$}). The three vertical distributions (2,000 data points each) correspond to $Z=0.014$ (the theoretical minimum $Z$ value), $Z=1$ (the monodisperse case) and $Z=2.904$ (the theoretical maximum $Z$ value). Insert: $\lambda$ \textit{vs} $Z$.}
