\section*{Ethic Considerations}

This paper focuses on dataset auditing in Deep Learning (DL). The objective of this paper is to advance the understanding of dataset auditing and evaluate the robustness and distinctiveness of existing methods from an adversarial perspective, which is critical to ensuring the transparency and trustworthiness of dataset auditing methods. Our paper intends to warn the community that existing dataset auditing methods may not be reliable under adversarial settings. All datasets used in our papers are publicly available. We also do not use any personally identifiable information or sensitive data. 



