% % This study's methodology synergizes the concept of distribution-aware adversarial testing with the computational efficiency of the ARO algorithm, creating a unique testing framework that produces adversarial examples which are both physically constrained and adept at uncovering potential vulnerabilities within the model. By embedding physical plausibility directly into the adversarial examples, this approach ensures that each test is relevant and applicable to real-world scenarios, particularly within the intricacies of ICPS. Furthermore, by harmonizing global data insights with detailed local and regional characteristics analysis, the HERO framework significantly enhances the understanding and evaluation of model performance.
% % This integration not only exposes the TSTransformer model's behavior under targeted conditions but also furnishes crucial insights for the continuous improvement and strategic development of future predictive models. Through its comprehensive and innovative approach, this methodology 
% The proposed underscores the critical role of physical constraints in the reliability and applicability of adversarial testing. It provides a pathway for refining and optimizing of models within the challenging landscape of industrial applications.


