Next, we prove that $D_2$ is an LD-set of $G$. Note that $D_2$ is a dominating set of $G$, as it is a dominating set of $G'$. For the sake of contradiction, assume that $D_2$ is not an LD-set of $G$. This implies that adding back the deleted edges has created some problem. Hence, there exists $y\in V(G)$ such that $N_{G}(y)\cap D_2=N_G(c)\cap D_2$. This implies that $N_{G'}(y)\cap D_2=(N_{G'}(c)\cap D_2)\setminus \{a\}$, implying $N_{G'}(y)\cap D_2=N_{G'}(x)\cap D_2$ which contradicts the fact that $D_2$ is an LD-set in $G'$. Hence $D_2$ is an LD-set in $G$. So $[D_1,D_2]$ is an LD-partition of $G$.


