\subsection{Unified Evaluation of ABPI and CPINN-ABPI} 
Here, we outline our evaluation of ABPI and CPINN-ABPI using simulation and real hardware data. After collecting the thermal traces from HotSpot and the Jetson Xavier board, each dataset is processed to align the power and temperature samples in a uniform 1-second interval. Initially, ABPI is applied independently to each platform to compute the thermal matrices \( A \) and \( B \) for the Jetson board and the simulated heterogeneous SoC. Using these parameters, the estimated power consumption for each unit is calculated and compared with the ground truth power measurements obtained from the onboard sensors in the real hardware and from the CoMeT simulator in the simulation environment~\cite{CoMet}. Subsequently, the proposed CPINN-ABPI approach is applied to both SoCs. The power predictions from CPINN-ABPI are then compared with those of ABPI to assess improvements in estimation accuracy, validating the effectiveness of the proposed method in both real and simulated scenarios. 


