\begin{equation*}
	\delta=\;\pm\frac{1}{2},\;\pm1,\;\pm2.
\end{equation*}
(cf. \cite[Proposition\cspace8(i), \S\phantom{.}1.3, Ch.\phantom{.}VI]{bourbaki}). A root $\alpha$ for which $\frac{1}{2}\alpha\notin R$ is said \emph{indivisible}, and a root system entirely consisting of indivisible roots is called \emph{reduced}.
