    Let $c\in\N^+$ be the least common multiple of $b_1,\ldots,b_{l-1}$. Since each $c\cdot\frac{a_i}{b_i}\in\Z$, \eqref{eq.1 - direction 2->1 lemma characterization of reflections} yields the trivial $\Z$-linear combination:
	\begin{equation*}
    \begin{split}
        0&=c\left(\frac{a_1}{b_1}x_1+\frac{a_2}{b_2}x_2+\ldots+\frac{a_{l-1}}{b_{l-1}}x_{l-1}\right)\\
