\subsection{Retrieval vs.\ Generation Strategy}
\label{subsec:retrieval_vs_generation}

We compared retrieval, generation, and hybrid strategies for image provisioning (Table~\ref{tab:retrieval_generation}). Retrieval is fastest (0.15s, 0.71 cosine, 2.3\% hallucination), generation is slowest (6.8s, 0.75 cosine, 12.5\% hallucination), and our hybrid approach achieves the best balance (2.4s, 0.80 cosine, 5.1\% hallucination). This confirms the hybrid method effectively balances speed, accuracy, and reliability for scalable multimodal QA.

